    "q-97115": {
      "dom_id": "step-q97115",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "$$\n[T]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,{P}_{C\\to B}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $[T]_{C}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to the basis $C$ and the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{C\\to B}$ shown above. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $B.$",
      "worked_solution": "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14163453/assets/2e82c232614bec8a98f079ea56d7913ee13e7b457e33e418198278d2e369fc5c.png)\n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}.\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{C\\to B}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B.$\n\nOur goal is to compute $[T]_{B}.$ Solving this equation for $[T]_{B},$ we obtain the alternative formulation\n\n$$\n[T]_{B}={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{C\\to B}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{C\\to B}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-1)\\cdot (-5)-3\\cdot 2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{B} & ={P}_{C\\to B}\\cdot [T]_{C}\\cdot {P}_{C\\to B}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
